[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[31m-# Incident 1, step 1.1 -- the probe Timur copied out of a blog post.\u001b[39m\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Incident 1, step 1.2 -- Ruslan fixes production the way Ruslan fixes production.\u001b[39m\u001b[18X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# The service takes 30 seconds to warm up. The probe starts asking after 5, and\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# gives up after three misses at 5-second intervals. 5 + 3x5 = 20 seconds of\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# patience against 30 seconds of startup. Nothing here is a bug, and the pod\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# dies every single time.\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# 25 is bigger than 15, the CrashLoop stops, and the fix holds until the day the\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# service starts taking longer. It is a bet that tomorrow looks like today.\u001b[39m\u001b[25X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#\u001b[39m\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# These numbers used to be 40 against 30. They are half that now because the\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# failure is pure arithmetic -- initialDelay + failureThreshold x period against\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# the warmup -- and arithmetic is as true at 25 s"]
[0.000, "o", "econds as at 40. What the\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# halving bought is most of a minute of stage time, which the theory cards now\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# spend explaining the probe while the rollout settles.\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#\u001b[39m\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Green here:  warmup 15 < initialDelay 25, ten seconds of margin.\u001b[39m\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Broken next: the step sets WARMUP_SECONDS=50 against 25 + 3x5 = 40 seconds of\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# patience, so the kill lands at 40 and the pod would have been ready at 50.\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n   apiVersion: apps/v1\u001b[81X\r\n   kind: Deployment\u001b[84X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -32,5 +40,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[78X\u001b[24;13H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cenv:\u001b[86X\u001b[25;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: WARMUP_SECONDS\u001b[66X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"30\"\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"15\"\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\u001b[28;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: HEALTHZ_MODE\u001b[68X\u001b[29;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"local\"\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -44,5 +52,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[78X\u001b[31;13H\u001b[1K\u001b[ClivenessProbe:\u001b[76X\u001b[32;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[ChttpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\u001b[49X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[12X\u001b[12CinitialDelaySeconds: 5\u001b[39m\u001b[66X\r\n  \u001b[32"]
[0.000, "o", "m+\u001b[12X\u001b[12CinitialDelaySeconds: 25\u001b[39m\u001b[65X\u001b[35;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CperiodSeconds: 5\u001b[72X\u001b[36;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CtimeoutSeconds: 1\u001b[71X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mTwenty-five is bigger than fifteen. We are done here.\u001b[39m\u001b[30X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mWhat if the start gets slower?\u001b[39m\u001b[53X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mWhy would it?\u001b[39m\u001b[70X\u001b[40;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ envsubst < k8s/incident1/11-liveness-initialdelay.yaml | kubectl apply -f -\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[24X\r\n  deployment.apps/svc configured\u001b[71X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mIt holds because nothing changed. Not because the number is right.\u001b[39m\u001b[17X\u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
