[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2msame manifest, slower environment\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[68X\r\n  \u001b[2mready \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1/1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . restarts \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . nodes \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . 46s . [->] click to move on\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39X\r\n  svc-7fc46f7645-rrfrs\u001b[11X\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\u001b[11C1/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\u001b[6;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n====================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n  initialDelaySeconds is a bet that tomorrow looks like today.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[41X\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n====================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[10;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mMay I? The documentation has a startupProbe.\u001b[39m\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mYou read the documentation?\u001b[39m\u001b[56X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAll of it.\u001b[39m\u001b[73X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37m...\u001b[39m\u001b[80X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "m \u001b[37mUntil startup says ready, liveness and readiness are not consulted at all.\u001b[39m         \r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mSo the start gets its own time budget?\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mIts own. Two minutes if it wants. It does not affect the liveness period.\u001b[39m\u001b[10X\u001b[18;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mwhat changes: 11-liveness-initialdelay.yaml -> 12-startup-probe.yaml\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[33X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -1,16 +1,14 @@\u001b[39m\u001b[84X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Incident 1, step 1.2 -- Ruslan fixes production the way Ruslan fixes production.\u001b[39m\u001b[18X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Incident 1, step 1.2, second half -- Madina read the documentation.\u001b[39m\u001b[31X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# 25 is bigger than 15, the CrashLoop stops, and the fix holds until the day the\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# service starts taking longer. It is a bet that tomorrow looks like today.\u001b[39m\u001b[25X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# startupProbe gives the slow start its own budget: 60 checks at 2 seconds is\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# two minutes of patience, and while it runs, liveness"]
[0.000, "o", " is not consulted at all.\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# The liveness numbers can then be about steady-state health, which is the only\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# thing they were ever meant to be about.\u001b[39m\u001b[59X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# These numbers used to be 40 against 30. They are half that now because the\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# failure is pure arithmetic -- initialDelay + failureThreshold x period against\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# the warmup -- and arithmetic is as true at 25 seconds as at 40. What the\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# halving bought is most of a minute of stage time, which the theory cards now\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# spend explaining the probe while the rollout settles.\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[31m-#\u001b[39m\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Green here:  warmup 15 < initialDelay 25, ten seconds of margin.\u001b[39m\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Broken next: the step sets WARMUP_SECONDS=50 against 25 + 3x5 = 40 seconds of\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# patience, so the kill lands at 40 and the pod would have been ready at 50.\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# WARMUP_SECONDS is 50 rather than 15 on pu"]
[0.000, "o", "rpose, and it has to match the value\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# the previous step broke the service with: the point of this step is that the\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# same slow start that was being punished a minute ago is now simply waited for.\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# It used to say 30 here while the script claimed 60 out loud, which made the\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[39m\u001b[100X\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[31m-# service starts taking longer. It is a bet that tomorrow looks like today.\u001b[39m\u001b[25X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# startupProbe gives the slow start its own budget: 60 checks at 2 seconds is\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# two minutes of patience, and while it runs, liveness is not consulted at all.\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# The liveness numbers can then be about steady-state health, which is the only\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# thing they were ever meant to be about.\u001b[39m\u001b[59X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# These numbers used to be 40 against 30. They are half that now because the\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# failure is pure arithmetic -- initialDelay + failureThreshold x period against\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# the warmup -- and arithmetic is as true at 25 seconds as at 40. What the\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# halving bought is most of a minute of stage time, which the theory cards now\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# spend explaining the probe while the rollout settles.\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[31m-#\u001b[39m\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Green here:  warmup 15 < initialDelay 25, ten seco"]
[0.000, "o", "nds of margin.\u001b[39m\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Broken next: the step sets WARMUP_SECONDS=50 against 25 + 3x5 = 40 seconds of\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# patience, so the kill lands at 40 and the pod would have been ready at 50.\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# WARMUP_SECONDS is 50 rather than 15 on purpose, and it has to match the value\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# the previous step broke the service with: the point of this step is that the\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# same slow start that was being punished a minute ago is now simply waited for.\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# It used to say 30 here while the script claimed 60 out loud, which made the\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# apply quietly undo the breakage the step was built on.\u001b[39m\u001b[44X\r\n   apiVersion: apps/v1\u001b[81X\r\n   kind: Deployment\u001b[84X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -40,5 +38,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[78X\u001b[25;13H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cenv:\u001b[86X\u001b[26;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: WARMUP_SECONDS\u001b[66X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"15\"\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"50\"\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\u001b[29;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: HEALTHZ_MODE\u001b[68X\u001b[30;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"local\"\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -50,"]
