[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[37mBlack Friday. The work arrives -- as a queue, which is what the whole system was built for.\u001b[39m\u001b[10X\u001b[3;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kubectl -n demo get scaledobject worker\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[60X\r\n  NAME     SCALETARGETKIND      SCALETARGETNAME   MIN   MAX   READY   ACTIVE   FALLBACK   PAUSED   TRIG\r\nGERS        AUTHENTICATIONS   AGE\u001b[70X\r\n  worker   apps/v1.Deployment   worker\u001b[12X\u001b[12C0     24    True    False    False      False    aws-\r\nsqs-queue   sqs\u001b[15X\u001b[15C11s\u001b[70X\u001b[9;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mKEDA watches the queue. Zero workers right now, because there is nothing to do.\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[1m> load: 20 rps, enqueue (panel bottom right)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[57X\r\n  \u001b[37mFilling the queue: two thousand messages a second going in.\u001b[39m\u001b[42X\u001b[13;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mKEDA, AND WHAT IT IS COUNTING\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m pollingInterval 5   it asks SQS how deep the queue is\u001b[46X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m queueLength 20      messages per worker it is willing to tolerate\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m maxReplicaCount 24  the ceiling, and the only thin"]
[0.000, "o", "g stopping it\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m desired workers = queue depth / 20, capped at 24.\u001b[50X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m minReplicaCount is 0, so this scales up from nothing at all.\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Nothing in that formula knows why the queue is deep. A queue that\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because the workers are stuck looks exactly like a queue that\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because there is a lot of work.\u001b[62X\u001b[25;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[31m\u001b[1m[>_<] KEDA     \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mQueue is deep. Adding workers.\u001b[39m\u001b[53X\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m[$_$] Karpenter\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mPods are Pending. Buying machines.\u001b[39m\u001b[49X\u001b[28;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue depth up, workers up, nodes up\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[65X\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0/0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . workers \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0/0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . nodes \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m ~$0.02/h . 80s . [->] click to move on\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[29X\u001b[31;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kubectl get nodes -l role=demo\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[69X\r\n  NAME\u001b[44X\u001b[44CSTATUS   ROLES    AGE     VERSION\u001b[20X\r\n  ip-10-42-17-219.eu-central-"]
