[0.000, "o", "[m\u001b[58X\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n====================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[35;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mEvery replica opens its own pool. Four connections each.\u001b[39m\u001b[27X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd every replica scans two million rows every two seconds, because that is what\u001b[39m   \r\n        \u001b[37mits readiness probe does.\u001b[39m\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThat is a health check.\u001b[39m\u001b[60X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThat is a health check multiplied by the replica count.\u001b[39m\u001b[28X\u001b[41;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mAt three replicas it was a third of a core. KEDA is allowed twenty-four.\u001b[39m\u001b[29X\r\n  \u001b[35m\u001b[1m(~_~) Postgres \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mTwenty-four workers at four connections is ninety-six. I have fifty-seven.\u001b[39m         \u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
