[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[37mFilling the queue: two thousand messages a second going in.\u001b[39m\u001b[42X\u001b[3;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mKEDA, AND WHAT IT IS COUNTING\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m pollingInterval 5   it asks SQS how deep the queue is\u001b[46X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m queueLength 20      messages per worker it is willing to tolerate\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m maxReplicaCount 24  the ceiling, and the only thing stopping it\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m desired workers = queue depth / 20, capped at 24.\u001b[50X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m minReplicaCount is 0, so this scales up from nothing at all.\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Nothing in that formula knows why the queue is deep. A queue that\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because the workers are stuck looks exactly like a queue that\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because there is a lot of work.\u001b[62X\u001b[15;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[31m\u001b[1m[>_<] KEDA     \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mQueue is deep. Adding workers.\u001b[39m\u001b[53X\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m[$_$] Karpenter\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mPods are Pending. Buying machines.\u001b[39m\u001b[49X"]
