[0.000, "o", ") Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd every replica scans two million rows every two seconds, because that is what\u001b[39m   \r\n        \u001b[37mits readiness probe does.\u001b[39m\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThat is a health check.\u001b[39m\u001b[60X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThat is a health check multiplied by the replica count.\u001b[39m\u001b[28X\u001b[36;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mAt three replicas it was a third of a core. KEDA is allowed twenty-four.\u001b[39m\u001b[29X\r\n  \u001b[35m\u001b[1m(~_~) Postgres \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mTwenty-four workers at four connections is ninety-six. I have fifty-seven.\u001b[39m         \r\n  \u001b[35m\u001b[1m(~_~) Postgres \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd two vCPU, which are now entirely yours.\u001b[39m\u001b[40X\u001b[40;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kubectl exec -n demo deploy/dbshell -- sh -c \"psql \\\"\\$DSN\\\" -c \\\"SELECT state, count(*),\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[10X\r\n    \u001b[36m\u001b[1mmax(now()-query_start)::interval(0) AS longest FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[25X\r\n    \u001b[36m\u001b[1mdatname=current_database() GROUP BY state ORDER BY 2 DESC"]
