[0.000, "o", "m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd a worker that cannot reach the database does not delete its message.\u001b[39m\u001b[11X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThe message comes back. The queue gets deeper.\u001b[39m\u001b[37X\r\n  \u001b[31m\u001b[1m[>_<] KEDA     \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mQueue is deeper. Adding workers.\u001b[39m\u001b[51X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThat is the loop.\u001b[39m\u001b[66X\u001b[34;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina's notes\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1m. THE LOOP\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m probe asks the DB  ->  replicas NotReady  ->  workers stop consuming\u001b[31X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m   ^\u001b[53X\u001b[53C|\u001b[42X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m   |\u001b[53X\u001b[53Cv\u001b[42X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m  more nodes bought  <-  KEDA adds workers  <-  queue depth grows\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Every turn adds connections to the database that is already the\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m bottleneck, which makes the next turn worse. Nothing in the loop\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m is broken. Every component is doing exactly what it was asked.\u001b[37X\u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
