[0.000, "o", "m  more nodes bought  <-  KEDA adds workers  <-  queue depth grows\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Every turn adds connections to the database that is already the\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m bottleneck, which makes the next turn worse. Nothing in the loop\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m is broken. Every component is doing exactly what it was asked.\u001b[37X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m The only part of it with a price tag is the bottom left.\u001b[43X\u001b[24;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2mthroughput at zero, nodes still climbing\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[61X\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0/0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . workers \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0/4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . nodes \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m ~$0.02/h . 115s . [->] click to move on\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n  worker-7dc9f7b67d-2cwsh        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  ContainerCreating R:0\u001b[44X\r\n  worker-7dc9f7b67d-fkbh4        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\r\n  worker-7dc9f7b67d-gz9k9        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\r\n  worker-7dc9f7b67d-qzq6r        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\u001b[32;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kube"]
[0.000, "o", "ctl -n demo get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=svc -o\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n    \u001b[36m\u001b[1mcustom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,READY:.endpoints[*].conditions.ready\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n  NAME        READY\u001b[84X\r\n  svc-pr7cl   true,true,false\u001b[74X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mNo endpoints left in the Service. Not one.\u001b[39m\u001b[41X\r\n  \u001b[2m# load stopped\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[87X\u001b[39;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n====================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n  Scaling did not save the service. Scaling is what took it down -- and it bought hardware to do it.\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n====================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[43;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?2026l"]
