[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mUnhook the probe from the database.\u001b[39m\u001b[48X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mA background goroutine does SELECT 1 every two seconds with a timeout and stores\u001b[39m   \r\n        \u001b[37mthe result in a flag.\u001b[39m\u001b[74X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThe probe reads the flag. That is all.\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd if the database really does go down?\u001b[39m\u001b[43X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThe flag goes stale and the pod honestly leaves the load balancer.\u001b[39m\u001b[17X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAll sixteen at once?\u001b[39m\u001b[63X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mOne at a time, as each flag expires. And the database gets not one extra query.\u001b[39m    \u001b[11;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mThe probe now costs O(1). Sixteen replicas or a hundred and sixty, it is the same.\u001b[39m\u001b[19X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "37mTwo more things. The pool is budgeted against the wall: three connections, not\u001b[39m     \r\n        \u001b[37mfour.\u001b[39m\u001b[90X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd KEDA gets a ceiling. An autoscaler without one is a way to turn an incident\u001b[39m    \r\n        \u001b[37minto an invoice.\u001b[39m\u001b[79X\u001b[17;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mwhat changes: 20-ready-db-each-call.yaml -> 21-ready-cached.yaml\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -1,17 +1,18 @@\u001b[39m\u001b[84X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# Incident 2, step 2.1 -- the readiness probe that passed review.\u001b[39m\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Incident 2, step 2.4 -- the fix, and three separate lessons in it.\u001b[39m\u001b[32X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# \"Readiness should verify we can actually read our data.\" Nobody argues with\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# that in a pull request, and at three replicas nobody notices: a scan every two\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# seconds, three times over, is a rounding error on the database.\u001b[39m\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# 1. READY_MODE=cached. One background refresher per replica does one cheap\u001b[39m\u001b[25X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    ping per inter"]
[0.000, "o", "val; the probe reads a flag. The cost is O(1) whatever the\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    replica count, which is the only property that survives autoscaling.\u001b[39m\u001b[27X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# The cost is replicas x (1/period). That is the entire incident. Everything that\u001b[39m\u001b[19X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# follows is arithmetic.\u001b[39m\u001b[76X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# 2. The pool is budgeted against the wall instead of ignoring it. 12 workers\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    at 3 connections plus 3 api replicas at 3 is 45, against the 54 the\u001b[39m\u001b[28X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    database will actually give us. The number was always knowable.\u001b[39m\u001b[32X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# The worker is scaled by KEDA on queue depth, from zero. Its pool is four\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# connections per replica. The database has 60, of which RDS keeps 4 for itself\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# and 2 more are held back for the observer -- 54 are actually available.\u001b[39m\u001b[27X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# maxReplicaCount is 24 here, so the ceiling is 24x4 = 96 worker connections\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# plus 3x4 from the api aga"]
[0.000, "o", "inst a budget of 54. The wall is not a risk, it is\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# a schedule.\u001b[39m\u001b[87X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# 3. maxReplicaCount is 12, not 24. An autoscaler with no ceiling is a way to\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    convert an incident into an invoice -- and on this account, into a real\u001b[39m\u001b[24X\r\n  \u001b[32m+#    one. Karpent\u001b[39m\u001b[83X\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l\u001b[10D\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: HEALTHZ_MODE\u001b[68X\u001b[3;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"local\"\u001b[72X\u001b[4;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: READY_MODE\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"db_each_call\"\u001b[39m\u001b[65X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"cached\"\u001b[39m\u001b[71X\u001b[7;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: QUEUE_URL\u001b[71X\u001b[8;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: ${QUEUE_URL}\u001b[67X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -69,5 +70,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[78X\u001b[10;13H\u001b[1K\u001b[CreadinessProbe:\u001b[75X\u001b[11;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[ChttpGet: { path: /ready, port: 8080 }\u001b[51X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[12X\u001b[12CperiodSeconds: 2\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[12X\u001b[12CperiodSeconds: 5\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\u001b[14;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CtimeoutSeconds: 1\u001b[71X\u001b[15;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CfailureThreshold: 3\u001b[69X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -102,5 +103,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[76X\u001b[17;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"200\"\u001b[74X\u001b[18;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: POOL_MAX\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"4\"\u001b[39m\u001b[76X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"3\"\u001b[39m\u001b[76X\u001b[21;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: CONCURRENCY\u001b[69X\u001b[22;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"2\"\u001b[76X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -108,5 +109,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[76X\u001b[24;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: \"local\"\u001b[72X\u001b[25;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: READY_MODE\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"db_each_call\"\u001b[39m\u001b[65X\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[14X\u001b[14Cvalue: \"cached\"\u001b[39m\u001b[71X\u001b[28;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- name: QUEUE_URL\u001b[71X\u001b[29;17H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cvalue: ${QUEUE_URL}\u001b[67X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -128,5 +129,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[76X\u001b[31;13H\u001b[1K\u001b[CreadinessProbe:\u001b[75X\u001b[32;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[ChttpGet: { path: /ready, port: 8080 }\u001b[51X\r\n  \u001b[31m-\u001b[12X\u001b[12CperiodSeconds: 2\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[32m+\u001b[12X\u001b[12CperiodSeconds: 5\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\u001b[35;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CtimeoutSeconds: 1\u001b[71X\u001b[36;15H\u001b[1K\u001b[CfailureThreshold: 3\u001b[69X\r\n  \u001b[36m@@ -152,5 +153,5 @@\u001b[39m spec:\u001b[76X\r\n       name: worker\u001b[84X\r\n     minReplicaCount: 0\u001b[80X\r\n  \u001b[31m-  maxReplicaCount: 24\u001b[39m\u001b[79X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  maxReplicaCount: 12\u001b[39m\u001b[79X\r\n     pollingInterval: 5\u001b[80X\r\n     cooldownPeriod: 30\u001b[80X\u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
